  "description": "HOSGAZ crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C24 H24 Ce4 N4 O36 8-,20(H2 O1),8(K1 1+). From the CIF bond table, Ce1 (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Ce2 (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Ce3 (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Ce4 (Ce) has 9 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 4 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.528-4.085 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 96.54-121.59°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula K8[Ce2(O2)3(NTA)2]2·20H2O. Article name explicitly identifies I(V).",
